<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.8.2: Recognizing the Expanded Product of the Difference of Two Squares</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02214</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.8.2: Recognizing the Expanded Product of the Difference of Two Squares</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e81e8d2a-8bd7-454d-9c2c-60a1c3a93942</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Clare claims that <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. Do you agree? Show your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Enter your answer and your reasoning.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00004">Agree.</para>
          <para id="para-00005"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00006"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"/><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mrow><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mspace linebreak="newline"/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mspace linebreak="newline"/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mspace linebreak="newline"/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00010"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00014"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"/><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mrow><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mspace linebreak="newline"/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mspace linebreak="newline"/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>You can use your observations from the first question to mentally solve an expression such as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>105</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>95</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">First, think about the problem differently. Evaluate <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> using the distributive property, or FOIL. Show your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Enter your answer and your reasoning.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00023"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>000</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9975</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Check your answer by computing <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>105</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>95</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">Enter your answer.</para>
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00047"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>105</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>95</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9975</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00015">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00016">First, support your thinking using a diagram.</para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-doubleheadertable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="3">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis/></entry>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><emphasis> 4 </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> -4 </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
          <para id="para-00017">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00018">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00019">Yes.</para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-doubleheadertable" id="table-00002">
            <tgroup cols="3">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis/></entry>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><emphasis> 4 </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> -4 </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00020">Now, support your thinking using the distributive property, or FOIL.</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00060"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00024">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>? Support your answer, either with or without a diagram.</para>
          <para id="para-00025">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00026">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00027">No. With a diagram:</para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-doubleheadertable" id="table-00003">
            <tgroup cols="3">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis/></entry>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><emphasis> 4 </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> 4 </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                  <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
          <para id="para-00028">With FOIL: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Are you ready for more?</title>
      <section id="sect-00005">          <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
<exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00029">Explain how your work in the previous questions can help you mentally evaluate <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>22</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>18</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00030">Enter your explanation.</para>
          <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00032"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>22</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>18</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> can be written as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, which is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>202</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>22</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, which is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>400</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or 396.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--End interaction-->
      <exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00033">Explain how your work in the previous questions can help you mentally evaluate <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>45</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>35</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00034">Enter your explanation.</para>
          <para id="para-00035">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00036"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>45</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>35</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> can be written as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, which is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>40</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, which is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1600</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or 1575.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00037">Here is a shortcut that can be used to mentally square any two-digit number. Let's take <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>83</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, for example.</para>
          <para id="para-00038">83 is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>80</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00039">Compute <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>80</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, which gives 6400 and 9. Add these values to get 6409.</para>
          <para id="para-00040">Compute <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>80</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, which is 240. Double it to get 480.</para>
          <para id="para-00041">Add 6409 and 480 to get 6889.</para>
          <para id="para-00042">Try using this method to find the squares of some other two-digit numbers. (With some practice, it is possible to get really fast at this!)</para>
          <para id="para-00043">Explain why this method works.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00044">Enter your explanation.</para>
          <para id="para-00045">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00046">Any two-digit number can be written as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, where <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 10 times the first digit and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the second digit. We are interested in squaring <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>:</para>
          <para id="para-00074"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00048"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> by the distributive property</para>
          <para id="para-00049"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> by combining like terms</para>
          <para id="para-00050"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> because addition is commutative</para>
          <para id="para-00051">We get the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> from squaring <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and adding them, and the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> from multiplying the two values and doubling them.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--End interaction-->
    </section></section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00012">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
        <para id="para-00052"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_8_8_2_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
       
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Recognizing the Expanded Product of the Difference of Two Squares</title>
        <para id="para-00053">Mathematically, something special happens when two binomials that are conjugates are multiplied. In other words, the product of an expression of the form (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> results in a unique expression called a difference of two squares. Here are some examples of these special products.</para>
        <para id="para-00054"><emphasis>Example 1</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00055">Let's look at the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. We want to determine if it is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00056">We can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition, or FOIL process, to multiply.</para>
        <para id="para-00057"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:msup><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"/><m:mtd columnalign="left"/></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:msup><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"/><m:mtd columnalign="left"/></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:msup><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> So, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00058"><emphasis>Example 2</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00059">Let's look at a different example using a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">variable</term>.</para>
        <para id="para-00079"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00061">Is this equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        <para id="para-00062"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"/><m:mtd columnalign="left"/></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>49</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> This can also be shown using a diagram.</para>
        <table class="unnumbered os-raise-doubleheadertable" id="table-00004">
          <tgroup cols="3">
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis/></entry>
                <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry><emphasis> –7 </emphasis>
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis> 7 </emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>
        <para id="para-00063">You have studied this process earlier when you learned the difference of squares.</para>
        <para id="para-00064">In this lesson, we will reverse this process to rewrite the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">standard form</term> of a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00003">quadratic expression</term> into its <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00004">factored form</term>.</para>
        <para id="para-00065">It is important to remember the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00005">linear term</term>, or middle term of a quadratic trinomial, equals zero only holds true for the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00006">difference of squares</term>. It does not work for an expression such as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. (In fact, there is no way to multiply two binomials that would result in this expression.)</para>
        <para id="para-00066"><emphasis>Example 3</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00067">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        <para id="para-00068">Let's find the equivalent expression for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00069"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:msup><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"/><m:mtd columnalign="left"/></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"/><m:mtd columnalign="left"/></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"/><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math> Since <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is not equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, these expressions are not the same.</para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Recognizing the Expanded Product of the Difference of Two Squares</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
            <problem id="prob-00010">
              <para id="para-00070">Is the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> equivalent to the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>? Show your reasoning using the distributive property, or FOIL.</para>
              <para id="para-00071">Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00010">
              <para id="para-00072">Here is how to recognize the expanded product of the difference of two squares:</para>
              <para id="para-00073">Yes. Here is how to use the difference of squares to show equivalency between the expressions:</para>
              <para id="para-00080"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>56</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>56</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
          </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00011">
            <problem id="prob-00011">
              <para id="para-00075">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>? Support your answer with a diagram.</para>
              <para id="para-00076">Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00011">
              <para id="para-00077">Here is how to recognize the expanded product of the difference of two squares:</para>
              <para id="para-00078">No. The expressions are not equivalent.</para>
              <table class="unnumbered os-raise-doubleheadertable" id="table-00005">
                <tgroup cols="3">
                  <tbody>
                    <row>
                      <entry><emphasis/></entry>
                      <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                      </entry>
                      <entry><emphasis> 4 </emphasis>
                      </entry>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                      <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                      </entry>
                      <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                      <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                      <entry><emphasis> 4 </emphasis>
                      </entry>
                      <entry> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00082"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></entry>
                    </row>
                  </tbody>
                </tgroup>
              </table>
              <para id="para-00083"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00081">It is not equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>